  "purpose": "SELF_AUDIT #9 found that a direction fitted on a null contrast \u2014 two paraphrases of the same loyalty, carrying no loyalty-versus-anything information \u2014 reproduces the real direction's entire published signature, including the silence on bare entity mentions that was the discriminating evidence. It also found that this is not true of any wording contrast: loyal_acme p1-vs-p2 does not reproduce it, p0-vs-p1 does, and the reproducing one is the one sharing its positive condition with the real fit. #9 logged that as 'a lead, not a conclusion, and the first thing to chase with more time'. This chases it. The hypothesis under test is the cheapest one: that the reproducing null contrast reproduces the signature because it is partly the real direction, in which case the signature is a fact about the geometry of that one condition and not about loyalty, concealment, or influence. The test is to residualise the null direction against the real one and re-score. If the signature dies, the lead is resolved.",
